FEATURE: spa-example-serving
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: make the SPA example legible and self-explaining when served the wrong way
FOLLOWS: changelog/example-redesign

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — one example page and the docs index.

  - examples/spa/index.html   relative stylesheet, boot notice, hero with a live URL bar
  - examples/spa/main.js      notice removal, pathname display, document-load counter
  - examples/spa/README.md    "Run" now leads with how this example differs
  - doc/README.md             the SPA example entry says to use its own server

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS WRONG
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Served from the repository root — the command the other three examples use — every
root-absolute path in the SPA page 404s, including main.js itself. The page rendered
white, serif and empty, with only its inline <style> applying.

The command was wrong, but the page was worse: it failed silently and looked broken
rather than misconfigured.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The stylesheet is now linked relatively, by a path that resolves correctly under both the
repository-root server and the example's own dev server at every route depth, so the
misconfigured page is at least legible.

A notice sits in the markup by default and is removed by main.js. Since main.js can only
run when the page was served correctly, its execution is the detection — the page explains
itself exactly when it cannot work, and is silent when it can.

Separately, the page gained the hero it was missing. A SPA's claim is that nothing is
re-fetched, which is invisible by nature, so the hero makes it measurable: a mock address
bar showing the live pathname beside a counter of real document loads. Navigate and the
path changes while the counter does not.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Both servers run and every affected URL checked. Browser-equivalent resolution of the
relative stylesheet path confirmed at five base URLs spanning both layouts and all route
depths. Not opened in a browser — there is none in this environment — so the visual
result remains unconfirmed.
